  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "garden-gmail-triggers (stack network)",
      "items": [
        "Pages at /gmail-triggers/ on the garden host: an Access JWT of the garden's own application on every request, Fetch Metadata on every page and form, CSRF and Origin on every POST",
        "Polls Gmail every 2 minutes, metadata only; agents never see email bodies through it",
        "Its only bind mount is state/garden/gmail-triggers, which the app-server does not mount",
        "Never connects to the app-server; shares no directory with it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Garden executor (inside the app-server)",
      "items": [
        "garden/executor/run.mjs, installed by lettucectl up in /root/.letta/garden/executor and run by system cron every minute",
        "With --gmail-triggers, claims requests from /executor/v1/ with the stack's token; the tunnel never routes that path",
        "Runs letta cron add --once with an argument array; posts results, the agent list and a heartbeat",
        "Also answers the garden landing page's agent-list asks (not drawn)",
        "Agents can read its token: they can do what it does, which is no more than letta cron add"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Unchanged Lettuce",
      "items": [
        "One app-server connection, owned by the BFF; the scheduler fires the task on it",
        "Each run shows in the Tasks tab as 'Gmail: <rule>'",
        "The agent reads the mail through google-mcp (not drawn)",
        "The BFF writes the Google token when the person connects Google in Settings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "lettucectl (host)",
      "items": [
        "compose/gmail-triggers.yml behind the garden-gmail-triggers profile (needs google)",
        "Tunnel route ^/gmail-triggers(/|$) on the garden host to garden-gmail-triggers:8000; / to the garden landing page",
        "Generates GARDEN_EXECUTOR_TOKEN once per stack; installs and removes the executor with the profile",
        "check_gmail_triggers: one bind mount, no symlinks on its path, Google volumes read-only, hardened"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust notes",
      "items": [
        "Lettuce's Google token is read, never written: the access token is refreshed in memory only",
        "A claimed request is never offered twice: a lost turn beats a duplicate",
        "Left out: google-mcp, the garden landing page, the vault, the code editor"
      ]
    }
  ]
